+## Built State (2026-07-28)
+
+**Scope actually delivered** — flake stabilization per Ruling A. Every flake
+was closed by a hermetic **test-seam** fix: `packages/` is untouched by this
+feature. **0 tests quarantined.**
+
+### What was built
+- **Global-state isolation** (`tests/conftest.py`, two autouse fixtures):
+  - *config-cache reset.* `get_config()` memoises a `RemedyConfig`, and
+    `load_config()` resolves `data_dir` from `REMEDY_DATA_DIR` plus a
+    cwd-relative `remedy.toml`. A test setting that variable through
+    `monkeypatch` baked its temp path into the cache; `monkeypatch` restores
+    the environment but cannot undo the cache, so later tests in the same
+    xdist worker read a stale `data_dir`. Closed classes F-B, F-C, F-E.
+  - *cwd restore.* A test that `chdir`s and never returns leaves the process
+    in a temp directory; every later test reading a repo file by a RELATIVE
+    path then fails (`FileNotFoundError: 'scripts/remedy_smoke.sh'`). Closed
+    7 repo-scan ids.
+- **Per-worker runtime ports** (`tests/ports.py`, `worker_port()`, base
+  15173; six runtime modules). All workers previously bound the product
+  default 5173, so a test asserting a readiness FAILURE could reach another
+  worker's healthy server. Closed 11 of 13 F-A/F-D ids.
+- **Manifest identity freeze** (`test_run_manifest.py`,
+  `test_job_rerun_manifest.py`). A run manifest records Remedy's own worktree
+  identity, and any untracked entry sets `dirty`; with 24 workers sharing one
+  repo tree, a neighbour's file churn between reference and candidate flipped
+  `same_inputs`. Frozen per test to the value seen at test start — the real
+  value, via the seam the modules already used (`_patch_remedy_identity`).
+  Product behaviour (F012 drift detection) deliberately unchanged. Closed F-F.
+- **Ledger pin** raised 250 → 251 → 252 as registered work items were added,
+  always atomically with the feature file and STATUS line.
+
